# Exists for `pnpm/action-setup@v4`, which copies this file into the throwaway directory it
# installs pnpm into and then installs with its own bundled (older) pnpm.
#
# Since pnpm 11 the npm package ships `bin/pnpm` as a placeholder that a `preinstall` script
# replaces with the real native binary. pnpm blocks dependency build scripts by default, so without
# this line the action installs the placeholder, every workflow dies on
# `bin/pnpm: 4: Syntax error: ")" unexpected`, and the message points nowhere near the cause.
#
# `only-built-dependencies` is the pre-12 spelling on purpose: the pnpm reading this file is the one
# bundled inside the action, not the pnpm 12 this repo runs. Our own build allow-list lives in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml under `allowBuilds`.
only-built-dependencies[]=pnpm
